                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "First thing I did when starting the game was notice it didn't have controller support. But in doing so, I alt + Tabbed out, which caused the game to lock up. Had to struggle to close it without a mouse, since the game hijacked that, too... \r\n\r\nOnce rebooting it, it was... fine, I guess? It's a pretty standard bullet hell. My music tracks really don't feel like they're adding anything to it, other than the BGM. I could theoretically mute the game, and play music in the background, and it wouldn't feel any different. Mouse only controls meant having to reposition the thing over and over, which will get you killed way too often when the enemies just fly into you, Galaga-style. Enemy bullets are almost invisible in the particle effect malestrom you're trying to see through. On the whole, it's just not the most gripping experience. Half the time I wish the story would just shut up and let me play the game. It has the SuperHot issue of standing in my way and spouting expositional wank at me while I'd like to just plan another level, please.",
